BEYOND THE 8 FORMAL ITEMS (every web region reproduced — covenant #2/#5)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WeekSelector:        prev button, calendar + week-range label + Current badge, next (disabled on
                     current week); pure date math (web getWeekRange incl. the JS Sunday quirk).
SummaryHeroCards:    Total Distance / Total Drives / Energy Used / Charging Cost / CO₂ Saved hero cards
                     + optional Fun Fact, each with its web-over-week trend chip (positive-driven
                     arrow + color, energy/cost inverted).
DrivingSection:      Daily-distance TSBarChart; Avg Efficiency / Total Driving Time / Efficiency Change
                     (colored trend icon) / Drives tiles; Top-Drive card (Date/Distance/Duration/
                     Efficiency) with its own empty state.
ChargingSection:     Daily-energy TSBarChart; Sessions / Total Energy Added / Avg Charge Rate / Total
                     Cost tiles; Energy-vs-Last-Week delta chip.
BatteryHealthSection: Avg-start + Avg-end battery pills (level-colored bar); Avg Charge Gain / Charge
                     Sessions / Est. Range Added tiles.
AlertsSection:       total badge; empty state ("No alerts this week — everything looks great!"); per-
                     severity rows (severity-colored icon + count chip) + alert-distribution TSPieChart.
WeekOverWeekSummary: Distance / Drives / Energy / Cost / Efficiency / CO₂ stat cards, each with trend.
States:              every section renders real content; top-drive + alerts carry their own empty state
                     (ContentUnavailableView) — never a blank region.
Units:               the web WeeklyDigest computes in display units (km / kWh / Wh / minutes / %) from
                     the legacy drives/charging shape and hard-codes those labels; this surface
                     reproduces that arithmetic + labels number-for-number (matching the sibling
                     SummaryHeroCards/DrivingSection feature-view parity units) — no SI conversion is
                     applicable to this legacy surface. The Shared SI facade is still linked/available.
a11y/HIG (ADR-015):  accessibilityElement/label/isHeader on panels, cards, pills, charts; Dynamic Type
                     via Font.TS tokens; adaptive macOS/iPad/iPhone grids + header reflow; light/dark
                     via design-token colors.

